* Independently designed 1:1 current mirror with MOS gate selection.
* Uses ORIGINAL GF model names; w/l are meters, not open_pdks micron units.
* IREF and logic/LED rails belong to the external testbench.
.subckt pixel_driver led_k pwm vlogic bias gate pwm_b
* Reference / output mirror. Nominal IREF=100uA, W/L=10um/2um.
XREF bias bias 0 0 nmos_6p0 w=10u l=2u
XOUT led_k gate 0 0 nmos_6p0 w=10u l=2u
* NMOS pass device connects bias to gate during PWM on.
XPASS bias pwm gate 0 nmos_6p0 w=2u l=1u
* Clamp removes gate charge during PWM off; gate is not intentionally floating.
XCLAMP gate pwm_b 0 0 nmos_6p0 w=2u l=1u
* Transistor-level inverter creates PWM complement from the 3.3V control rail.
XINV_N pwm_b pwm 0 0 nmos_6p0 w=2u l=1u
XINV_P pwm_b pwm vlogic vlogic pmos_6p0 w=4u l=1u
.ends pixel_driver
